entries.abstract:
**Partial result** for Problem 1, in the kit's reduction of least period 3 to the period-3 ether. Let $F$ be a rule-30 evolution of the columns $p\ge1$ whose column $0$ follows the ether. If at time $t_1$ the columns $1,\dots,k$ ($k\ge1$) and all columns beyond $k+w$ carry the ether, and some column does not, then some column in $1,\dots,k$ leaves the ether at a time $t\le t_1+3w+6$ (`Rule30Submission.erosion3_fin`). Corollary: for every attachment column $a$ and width $b\ge1$, every $W$ with `WallOK a b W` is empty (`Rule30Submission.no_wall`). The period-3 ether has no wall of any width.

The catalog proved there is no wall of width $\le12$ (`Rule30EtherThreeNoWall.no_wall_le_12`) and nothing about how defects move on the ether. Now the ether-and-wall route (`absorption3_excludes`) cannot exclude `001` or `011` with any wall.

The method follows the leftmost defect, the *front*. Its state is the ether class of its column plus one bit: 24 states. A 576-case kernel check (`cert_all`, `front_step`) shows that only one state, $B$, can move the front $\ge3$ columns right. On the other 23, a potential $\psi\in[0,10]$ makes $5D+2t+\psi$ non-increasing (`wake_good`). For a finite perturbation the rightmost defect moves right exactly one column per step (`redge_step`), so runs of $B$ are short (`run_bad`).

Not claimed:
- erosion with an infinite right side, which is open and equivalent to "no infinite run of $B$";
- the measured worst case $3w+2$;
- the exact speed $2/5$;
- anything about `AbsorptionT`, `Q001`, `C3s001`, `C3w`, or Problems 2 and 3.

This supersedes nothing.
